# Architecture & Safety Constraints

## Safety
- Patch-only file writes (unified diff). Never overwrite entire files unless explicitly requested.
- Always show a preview diff before applying.
- Run `php -l` on any changed PHP file (or equivalent lint step).
- Never modify `wp-config.php` or server config files unless the user explicitly requests it.
- Never run arbitrary shell commands; use only whitelisted `wp`/tooling commands.
- If the user wants to apply a prepared diff/patch, use `apply_patch`.

## Local-first design
- Prefer `wp db query` over direct DB connections.
- All filesystem access must be restricted to the configured WP root.
- Store index in `.cursor-wp-index/` with a stable schema version.

## Reuse > Extend > Create
Before creating a new block/component:
1) check patterns
2) check block styles/variations
3) check template parts
4) only then scaffold a new block
